    "diagnosisMethod": "Clinical interview: symptom type (nasal vs. ocular vs. pharyngeal), onset season and trigger pattern, geographic location (Central Valley — tree/grass pollen; coastal — maritime grasses; Southern California — eucalyptus, olive, mulberry), temporal course, response to prior OTC antihistamines, comorbid asthma status, nasal polyp history, aspirin sensitivity (Samter's triad assessment). Video nasal exam guided by patient (exterior nasal appearance, any visible swelling or deformity).",
